Wait — there's an ordering subtlety. `ScrollView.children(...).modifiers(Frame...)` — modifiers innermost-first. In the original: `ScrollView.children(Navigation.container(router)).modifiers(Frame.ofWidth(...))` means the Frame modifier wraps the ScrollView children result. If I reorder to `.modifiers(Frame...)` first, then `.children(...)`, does the builder apply modifiers the same way?

Let me check ViewBuilder: it collects modifiers and children, and in render() applies modifiers to the view THEN children. Actually the ViewBuilder.render:
```java
if (!children.isEmpty() && view instanceof ChildrenView content) {
    content.setChildren(children);
}
View result = view;
for (ViewModifier modifier : modifiers) {
    result = Modified.apply(result, modifier);
}
return result.render(env);
```

So modifiers wrap the view (with the children set), regardless of call order. So `.modifiers(...)` before or after `.children(...)` on the builder yields the same result. Good — the operations are order-independent on the builder. So reordering is safe.

Now let me continue with kitchensink sections.

